BulkModulus

The Bulk Modulus

The bulk modulus of a substance quantifies the resistance of the substance to bulk compression.

K = -V \frac{\mathrm{d}P}{\mathrm{d}V}

where:

K [var. scal. BulkModulus] is the bulk modulus
V [var. scal. Volume] is the volume of the substance
P [var. scal. Pressure] is the pressure applied to the substance

